# Academic Research Practices

## Research Phase Guidelines (Weeks 1-8)
- Focus on literature review and methodology development
- Document all research decisions and rationale
- Maintain bibliography with proper citations using HARVARD citation format
- Use inline citations when possible and where needed in all texts
- Everything must be cited properly - no uncited claims or methodologies
- Track research gaps and opportunities
- Regular progress documentation and milestone tracking

## Evaluation Focus
- Implement both technical metrics (ROUGE, BERTScore) and educational quality assessments
- Bloom's taxonomy alignment analysis
- Pedagogical framework adherence
- Compare against general-purpose LLM baselines

## Academic Writing Standards
- Maintain academic writing standards for all documentation
- Include proper citations and references in all research work
- Structure documentation for academic audience
- Balance technical detail with accessibility
- Follow MSc-level academic expectations

## Course Materials Integration
**Weekly Lecture Notes Structure:**
The `@docs/course-materials/` directory contains structured weekly course content organized as:
- `unit-XX/` directories for each week's materials
- `unit-XX-topic-name.md` for core weekly content
- Supporting documents for methodologies, outlines, and additional materials
- Project proposal documents and revision plans

**When Working with Academic Content:**
- Reference course materials from `@course-materials` when providing academic guidance
- Check relevant unit content for methodological frameworks and requirements
- Align suggestions with academic standards and timelines covered in course units
- Consider progression of topics across units when making recommendations

**Integration Guidelines:**
- Search course materials for relevant methodological guidance before suggesting approaches
- Ensure recommendations align with MSc-level academic expectations outlined in units
- Use course terminology and concepts consistently across units
- Support dissertation development aligned with course progression

## Project Phase Awareness
Current phase information should be maintained in separate progress tracking files. AI should:
- Consider current project phase when making suggestions
- Prioritize tasks appropriate to current timeline
- Suggest phase-appropriate tools and approaches
- Help maintain academic project momentum

## Research Quality Standards
- All research should meet academic rigor standards
- Experiments should be reproducible and well-documented
- Results should be clearly presented and analyzed
- Contribute meaningfully to AI-education research field
